<http://data.silknow.org/object/a7101743-80b3-363e-afe7-2d3cb8dedc02>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tapestry-woven wool on a cotton warp. The serape is woven with wide stripes of red, green, and purple, each stripe having a zig-zag pattern in a different colour. In the centre is a large diamond-shaped ornament in red, with a pattern of smaller diamonds. The border is red with a green zig-zag, and is bound with a red silk braid, and at each end is a red silk fringe. The serape is made in two pieces, joined down the centre."@en , "Tapestry woven wool; Mexico; 1880s."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/dd72ce1d-198f-3368-b577-8cb9b2e6fe99> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Tapestry woven wool; Mexico; 1880s."@en , "Tapestry-woven wool on a cotton warp. The serape is woven with wide stripes of red, green, and purple, each stripe having a zig-zag pattern in a different colour. In the centre is a large diamond-shaped ornament in red, with a pattern of smaller diamonds. The border is red with a green zig-zag, and is bound with a red silk braid, and at each end is a red silk fringe. The serape is made in two pieces, joined down the centre."@en ;
